Description:
 linuxmuster-base7 - linuxmuster.net configuration scripts
Changes:
 linuxmuster-base7 (7.4.15) lmn74; urgency=low
 .
   * fix(ntp.conf): drop obsolete notrap restrict flag, which ntpsec
     ignores and logs on every start (#192, PR #193, debbab8).
   * fix(ntp.conf): drop obsolete nopeer restrict flag, same reason (7505cbc).
   * refactor(e_fstab.py): split main() into named phase functions (#129, 354ea1b)
   * refactor(import_devices.py): split main() into named step functions,
     drop dead devices/serverip/domainname variables (#129, 22b07aa)
   * refactor(import_subnets.py): split main() into readSetupValues(),
     partitionSubnets() and updateFirewall() (#129, 2d405f4)
   * refactor(setup.py): split main() into parseArguments(),
     openSetupLogfile(), writeCustomIni() and runSetupModules() (#129, e4c6e69)
   * refactor(functions.py): split into functions/ package with 8 cohesive
     submodules (core, files, network, samba, linbo, certs, remote,
     security); __init__.py re-exports every name unchanged (#129, 5f1841e)
   * fix(d_templates.py): fill @@restricted_subnets@@ with a safe empty
     default and create /var/log/ntpsec proactively - both were causing
     ntpd errors on the very first start of a fresh install (4873245)
   * fix(d_templates.py): run the one-time ntpd sync as ntpsec:ntpsec
     instead of root, avoiding an AppArmor dac_override denial that still
     caused "Permission denied" writing to /var/log/ntpsec (9cd111a)
